{"nodes": [{"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_figure", "label": "The spectra index \u2014 what is witnessed", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A three-panel reading of the index (2D plane, three.js lattice, obstacle bars) whose point is that every cell carries a grade and a source, so the index can state its own ignorance."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_spectra_index", "label": "The spectra index (101,328 cells)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cells on (Z, charge, \u2113, 2S+1); 337 witnessed, 929 exact by symmetry, 100,062 computed by the filler \u2014 0.333% checked against reality."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_staircase_admitted_set", "label": "Staircase admitted set", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Charge cannot exceed Z, so the admitted set is a staircase \u2014 which is why the index closes at E = 0 on these coordinates structurally rather than by discovery."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_grade_witnessed", "label": "Grade: witnessed", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reality has been consulted for that cell. 337 of 101,328 \u2014 the grade the whole index is calibrated against."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_grade_exact_by_symmetry", "label": "Grade: exact by symmetry", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "929 cells whose value follows from symmetry rather than from an observation or the filler."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_grade_computed_by_filler", "label": "Grade: computed by the filler", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "100,062 cells the filler supplies. Everything not witnessed or exact is theory, and the index says so rather than hiding it."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_named_obstacles", "label": "Named obstacles, not probabilities", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each unwitnessed cell carries the named obstacle standing between it and an observation \u2014 series above ng (28,527), no isotope (24,312), NOT KEYABLE (17,641), open core (16) (11,605), open core (3) (9,756), open core (119) (5,280), no analysis at charge (2,691), no primordial (5). A named obstacle may or may not be lifted; a probability cannot be."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_no_bound_queue", "label": "NO BOUND \u2014 the 245-cell working queue", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Cells with no bound at all: reachable and unread. This is the queue the index hands to collection."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_keyability", "label": "Keyability (register 1597)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A quantum defect needs a single 2S+1; a species with a hole plus an electron, or two valence electrons, yields only a multiplet mean. 17,641 cells fail the test \u2014 and applying it cut the NO BOUND queue from 2,929 to 245 at no cost but reading eight spectra already on disk."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_registers_1578_1597", "label": "Registers 1578\u20131597", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The register span the index figure cites as its provenance."}, {"id": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_lattice_view_z_charge_l", "label": "Lattice view (Z, charge, \u2113)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three coordinates at once as a three.js point cloud; yellow is witnessed, everything else coloured by the obstacle in the way."}], "edges": [{"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_figure", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_spectra_index", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "extracted/archives/restore-point-2-13/spectra-index.html", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectra_index_spectra_index", "target": "extracted_archives_restore_point_2_13_spectr